WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:02.990
Dr Zaretsky didn’t remember falling.

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:07.620
She’d hit her head on impact with the ground,
hard enough to knock the immediate memory

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:08.620
out of her brain.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:12.880
But not quite hard enough to remember everything
else.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:18.900
The feeling of mushy fungal fingers wrapping
around her waist, of rising rapidly into the

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:24.029
air, the haze of deadly spores so thick in
the air that they’d created a layer coating

00:00:24.029 --> 00:00:25.340
her hazmat suit.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:26.539
5 meters.

00:00:26.539 --> 00:00:29.560
That’s how far she’d fallen.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:32.489
About half the height of an Olympic diving
board.

00:00:32.489 --> 00:00:34.750
Only there wasn’t a pool at the bottom.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:36.860
And she’d landed badly.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:40.820
Dr Zaretsky had been lying in her hospital
bed for nearly a month.

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:47.879
It was rare to have an encounter with a 30-meter-tall
SCP go south and still live to tell the tale.

00:00:47.879 --> 00:00:53.180
She knew that as well as anyone, seeing colleagues
dying in all kinds of ways around her for

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:54.180
years.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:59.340
But try as she might, through all the broken
bones, all the bruises and scars, and all

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:05.340
the indignity that being bedridden in a hospital
brought, she couldn’t help but just feel

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:06.470
sad.

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:08.270
Were all these SCPs monsters?

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:13.110
And what was happening to 5771 as she lay
there broken?

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:14.110
*

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:19.729
It will be no surprise to many that the SCP
Foundation monitors emergency service calls.

00:01:19.729 --> 00:01:24.030
Often if there is a deadly creature on the
loose, the first people to hear about it are

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:26.380
emergency service operators.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:31.579
Whether they believe it is another case, something
that benefits the Foundation greatly much

00:01:31.579 --> 00:01:32.579
of the time.

00:01:32.579 --> 00:01:36.470
That was how SCP-5771 was discovered.

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:41.970
Bryce Wheeler, a junior agent not yet ready
for field work, was monitoring incoming 911

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:45.430
calls in California when a call pricked her
interest.

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:48.219
It wasn’t so much the content of the call
itself.

00:01:48.219 --> 00:01:53.130
It was the fact that it was the third call
that morning where someone had died on the

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:54.170
phone.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:59.750
As soon as the line connected, all that could
be heard were wheezing and choking noises.

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:03.560
The operator tried their best to reassure
the person that help was on its way, and they

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:08.170
were tracking the location of the call, but
it seemed to provide little comfort.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:13.170
The choking noises stopped, and there was
the familiar static thud of the phone and

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:14.920
body falling to the ground.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:18.750
Then the line just sat open, totally silent.

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:23.450
It made sense why the line was silent, as
Agent Wheeler looked at the tracking data

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:25.750
on where that call was coming from.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:29.110
It was a National Park; the middle of nowhere.

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:34.560
Chances were there wouldn’t be any emergency
services on the scene for a good hour at least.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:39.250
That gave the Foundation time to swing into
action, diverting any emergency services in

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:44.410
the area to other calls and creating sufficient
confusion within the emergency services to

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:48.970
file a couple of false response IDs so nobody
would ever notice.

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:54.159
That kind of thing was and is very standard
procedure for the Foundation at this point.

00:02:54.159 --> 00:02:58.220
Since Wheeler had caught the call, she was
given permission to ride along as they went

00:02:58.220 --> 00:02:59.530
to investigate.

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:04.500
She only had one piece of intel to pass on
to the senior agents as their SUV bumped its

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:10.550
way through the National Park, a choked word
that all three callers had said: ‘Mushroom’.

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:14.890
They stopped about a kilometer out from where
the call had come in from and got out of the

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:17.090
car to see their first body of the day.

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:20.920
There would be plenty more before the sun
would go down that night.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:23.950
It was a hiker, early twenties, in good shape.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:26.640
They’d evidently collapsed on the trail.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:30.840
Lying face down, there was a small drying
pool of saliva in the dirt.

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:33.060
Must have been coughing too.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:36.610
Agent Wheeler was just about to go over to
the body and roll it onto its back when one

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:39.459
of the other agents put a hand on her shoulder.

00:03:39.459 --> 00:03:42.810
This was potentially a biohazard situation.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:44.730
They could not risk getting infected.

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:47.470
They’d proceed in the vehicle with caution.

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:49.980
They passed three more bodies on the trail
as they went.

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:54.810
They reported each one back to the Foundation,
who were in the process of setting up a perimeter

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:59.920
around the National Park and combing the outskirts
looking for hikers for apprehension and medical

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:00.920
help.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:04.380
Once they’d passed their fifth body, the
driver stopped the car again.

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:08.680
He was leaning forwards in his seat, peering
up into the sky.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:12.560
Agent Wheeler tried her best to see what he
and all the others were looking up at but

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:13.790
couldn’t make it out.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:18.530
They were next to a little rocky canyon with
a few trees sticking up out of the ground,

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:22.259
most of them stripped nearly white by the
heat of the sun.

00:04:22.259 --> 00:04:25.900
Actually, there was one tree that looked taller
than the others.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:27.139
Thinner too.

00:04:27.139 --> 00:04:31.570
As she leaned forward in the seat and her
eyes saw more and more of the tree, she quickly

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:34.020
realized it wasn’t a tree at all.

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:40.570
It was a pair of spindly legs, then a skeletal
torso with gangly arms, then an elongated

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:43.250
neck, and then… a mushroom.

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:47.669
Without thinking, Agent Wheeler opened the
SUV’s door and stepped out into the California

00:04:47.669 --> 00:04:48.669
heat.

00:04:48.669 --> 00:04:53.259
She was tiny in comparison to the creature
before her, barely as tall as its ankle.

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:57.979
Its whole body seemed to be soft and slightly
wrinkled, just like the mushrooms you’d

00:04:57.979 --> 00:04:59.110
cook with at home.

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:04.690
Her mouth fell wide open as she stared up
at it, and to her surprise, it turned around

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:05.860
and stared back.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:10.130
It didn’t have eyes, a face, or any features
at all.

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:16.160
All there was was a giant mushroom for a head,
but somehow it seemed to ‘see’ her.

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:18.910
It leaned down and peered closely at her.

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:22.590
The agents in the car were yelling something
behind her, but she ignored them.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:28.320
There was something ancient about this creature
and yet something so young and innocent.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:29.350
She coughed.

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:30.880
Then coughed again.

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:33.810
Tiny spores were floating through the air
all around her.

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:38.760
Within three minutes, Agent Wheeler’s throat
had totally closed off, full of fungal growths.

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:42.750
The other agents tried to open fire on the
creature but were all dead just moments after

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:45.750
she was, all choked to death.

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:46.750
*

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:49.630
All told, the Foundation discovered 18 civilian
bodies that day.

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:52.940
Each was reported to their family as having
died of other causes.

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:55.450
No autopsies were allowed to be carried out.

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:59.650
Anyone who claimed to have seen any kinds
of mushrooms when interrogated that day were

00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:02.250
administered Class-A amnestics

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:06.949
The containment perimeter quickly tightened
as Foundation personnel moved in on this enormous

00:06:06.949 --> 00:06:08.350
Mushroom Man.

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:11.580
With heavy weaponry at the ready, the Foundation
surrounded the creature.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:16.030
It bent down on its approach with hands out
by its sides.

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:21.000
This was interpreted as an act of hostility,
and the SCP was secured swiftly and without

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.060
leniency.

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:26.819
A special containment cell had to be constructed
for the Mushroom Man as it was far too tall

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:28.750
for any standard cell.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:34.180
It was detained in an external holding area
until the 32-meter tall cell had completed

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:35.330
construction.

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:39.930
Once inside, the Foundation was able to get
to work studying it.

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:45.780
Designated SCP-5771, this SCP measures 30.48
meters in height.

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:50.550
Its organic tissue seems to be made up entirely
of a gargantuan fungal growth.

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:55.669
The ‘head’ of the creature resembles a
mushroom of the Amanita pantherina species,

00:06:55.669 --> 00:06:58.479
also known as the Panther Cap mushroom.

00:06:58.479 --> 00:07:01.949
The body resembles a rudimentary humanoid
skeleton.

00:07:01.949 --> 00:07:06.129
Samples taken from it have revealed that it
is composed of the mushroom’s stalk material,

00:07:06.129 --> 00:07:09.970
while the creature’s thorax is made up of
the ring of the fungus.

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:14.509
It has a keen awareness of external stimuli,
particularly living beings.

00:07:14.509 --> 00:07:18.380
A mouse in a cage was placed inside its cell
for one hour.

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:24.360
Unlike all of the humans exposed to 5771’s
spores, the mouse did not die or suffer any

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:26.660
form of fungal infection.

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:31.620
What was more notable, however, was 5771’s
response to the mouse.

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:35.980
Leaning in as close as it could, it appeared
to stare at the mouse for the entire time

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:41.560
that the mouse was in its cell, despite lacking
eyes or any obvious sensory organs.

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:47.530
Researchers noted an apparent air of curiosity
about the tiny creature, or at the very least,

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:48.880
a primitive interest.

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:51.460
5771 emits spores continuously.

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:55.360
When it moved into its holding cell, the room
filled with so many spores over the course

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:59.770
of the week that it was difficult to even
observe the creature through the cameras.

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:03.410
It was determined that the cell would have
to be cleaned twice a week.

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:09.770
To ascertain how safe this would be, D-2304
was sent into the cell in a level 2 hazmat

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:10.770
suit.

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:13.580
Within three minutes, the D-class personnel
was dead.

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:18.690
It was decided that level 4 hazmat suits were
required, and since then, there have been

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:22.350
no issues with infections of personnel from
the spores.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:24.690
This is where Dr. Zaretsky came in.

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:29.580
A keen Mycologist with a background in studying
the cordyceps genus, she had leaped at the

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:32.330
opportunity to study SCP-5771.

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:38.019
A particular breakthrough came when communication
was established with the Mushroom Man.

00:08:38.019 --> 00:08:43.550
Dr. Zaretsky had the idea of using biodata
sonification to try to look for any microcurrent

00:08:43.550 --> 00:08:51.550
fluctuations in SCP-5771; the same ones that
occur in non-anomalous living organisms.

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:56.250
To her and the research team’s surprise,
as soon as the electrodes were inserted into

00:08:56.250 --> 00:09:05.370
the SCP’s feet, a low, slow voice seemed
to appear in the static noise of the computers.

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:08.370
‘Nature…is…friend…

00:09:08.370 --> 00:09:11.370
Nature…is…friend…why?…’

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:15.779
Enthused by her breakthrough Dr. Zaretsky
set up an interview slot as soon as possible

00:09:15.779 --> 00:09:18.350
to talk to 5771.

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:23.090
It appeared to have a limited vocabulary,
but did not display any significant difficulties

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:24.620
in understanding her.

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:29.959
When asked where it came from, 5771 simply
replied, ‘Nature’.

00:09:29.959 --> 00:09:35.290
When asked for further specifics, it was only
able to add that it came from ‘Mother.’

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:40.400
Keen to understand what its purpose was, Dr.
Zaretsky changed tack, asking the mushroom

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:42.700
giant why it had been born.

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:44.230
Why was it here?

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:45.490
What did it want?

00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:50.339
On the surface, it appeared to ignore the
question, choosing to ask one of its own.

00:09:50.339 --> 00:09:53.370
‘Why… hurt… mother?’

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:58.079
Taken slightly aback by this, the Doctor tried
to clarify what it meant by them ‘hurting

00:09:58.079 --> 00:09:59.079
mother.’

00:09:59.079 --> 00:10:04.030
The creature was not referring to her specifically
but to humanity collectively.

00:10:04.030 --> 00:10:08.279
It appeared to use the words ‘mother’
and ‘nature’ fairly interchangeably, so

00:10:08.279 --> 00:10:12.740
Dr Zaretsky asked if it was referring to climate
change.

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:18.529
5771 seemed to confirm that, informing her
that ‘mother’ was hurting, asking why

00:10:18.529 --> 00:10:21.040
humans wanted to hurt mother.

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:26.940
Taking the offensive, Zaretsky asked 5771
why it had hurt and killed so many people

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:30.670
to which it simply said, ‘unintentional…

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:32.029
apologies…’

00:10:32.029 --> 00:10:36.440
It was then ascertained that the creature
has no conscious control over the release

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:38.430
of its deadly spores.

00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:44.070
Later assessment has also theorized that 5771
does not bend down towards humans as an attack

00:10:44.070 --> 00:10:49.720
to expose them to more spores, but is instead
trying to make itself less intimidating.

00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:54.360
It spent much of the rest of the interview
asking Dr. Zaretsky for forgiveness for its

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:55.360
actions.

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:59.680
The SCP seemed very keen to let her and the
other researchers know that it never meant

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:04.300
to hurt anybody and even demonstrated remorse
over its actions.

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:09.160
In an attempt to reassure the SCP, who seemed
to be growing more distressed by the minute,

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:12.850
Zaretsky accepted the apology and said that
they were friends.

00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:18.120
While it is difficult to tell if a mushroom
is joyful, researchers generally agreed that

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:21.870
was the displayed emotion at hearing those
words.

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:26.230
And perhaps that was Dr. Zaretsky’s big
mistake.

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:31.040
5771, so happy to have made a friend, attempted
to pick her up.

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:35.700
Wrapping its fungal fingers around her torso,
it lifted her straight off her feet and up

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:36.890
into the air.

00:11:36.890 --> 00:11:41.850
Zaretsky screamed, taken aback completely
and overcome with the fear of suffering the

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:46.279
same fate as the 18 civilians in the national
park.

00:11:46.279 --> 00:11:50.640
Realizing its mistake, the SCP dropped her
from a height of 5 meters.

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:54.889
She was rushed to the hospital with a broken
left wrist, fractures in her left ankle, left

00:11:54.889 --> 00:11:58.740
arm, and left elbow, and some other minor
sprain injuries.

00:11:58.740 --> 00:12:03.899
Out of action for two months, Dr. Zaretsky
had no contact with the SCP as she lay in

00:12:03.899 --> 00:12:05.320
her hospital bed.

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:08.110
Meanwhile, 5771 grew withdrawn.

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:12.139
It would hunker down in the corner of its
cell in an attempt to be as unthreatening

00:12:12.139 --> 00:12:13.540
as possible.

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:18.980
Equipped with a proximity alarm, Dr. Danielle
Baker took over the interview sessions.

00:12:18.980 --> 00:12:24.959
Asking sharp, direct questions, Dr. Baker
tried to understand why SCP-5771 had attacked

00:12:24.959 --> 00:12:26.060
her colleague.

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:30.110
The Mushroom Man, still crouched in the corner,
apologized profusely.

00:12:30.110 --> 00:12:34.870
It referred to Zaretsky as ‘friend’ and
repeatedly asked where she was with growing

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:35.870
distress.

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:41.010
Dr. Baker’s interview technique in this
session led her to be reprimanded by her supervisor.

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:45.850
She pushed the questions hard, interrogating
the creature as to why it had hurt the Doctor.

00:12:45.850 --> 00:12:50.230
It was only when her supervisor stepped in
that she relented, revealing that Zaretsky

00:12:50.230 --> 00:12:52.690
was alive and recovering well.

00:12:52.690 --> 00:12:58.190
As the interview concluded, 5771 had one request
for the departing doctor.

00:12:58.190 --> 00:12:59.790
‘Protect… friend…’

00:12:59.790 --> 00:13:03.730
Fortunately, none of Dr. Zaretsky’s injuries
were serious.

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:09.420
Within a few weeks, she was back in the cell
with 5771 conducting another interview session.

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:14.110
She barely entered the room and started to
talk before the SCP interrupted her with cries

00:13:14.110 --> 00:13:20.130
of ‘friend!’ and many sincerely offered
apologies for what it had done to her.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:24.420
The pair of them have conducted several interview
sessions since, many of which have been left

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:29.480
undocumented as they contain little relevant
data to help the Foundation understand this

00:13:29.480 --> 00:13:31.810
SCP or the wider world.

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:35.920
Much of Zaretsky’s conversations with the
creature revolve around ‘Mother.’

00:13:35.920 --> 00:13:42.230
No matter Zaretsky’s best efforts, 5771
seems unable to grasp why humans are hurting

00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:43.230
Mother.

00:13:43.230 --> 00:13:47.660
It uses the words ‘burned’, ‘drowned’,
‘poisoned’, and ‘tortured’ to describe

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:49.529
what is happening to Mother.

00:13:49.529 --> 00:13:53.290
It claims that this is the reason that it
was created.

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:59.300
Discussions between Dr. Zaretsky and her wider
research team have concluded that SCP-5771

00:13:59.300 --> 00:14:03.060
seems to have been created as a response to
the climate crisis.

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:07.589
Several have noted the Gaia theory as a part
of this finding, which claims that the Earth

00:14:07.589 --> 00:14:12.199
is essentially one giant self-regulating organism,
called Gaia.

00:14:12.199 --> 00:14:17.620
Humans, plants, and animals all play roles
equivalent to individual cells.

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:22.490
If one group overpopulates and begins to harm
Gaia, then the body as a whole takes steps

00:14:22.490 --> 00:14:26.000
to address the disturbance.

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:31.810
SCP-5771 is theorized to be one of those steps
being taken by Gaia, Mother Earth, Nature,

00:14:31.810 --> 00:14:37.900
or whichever title you prefer, in order to
address the problem of manmade climate change.

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:44.070
With the ability to empathize, communicate,
and forgive, 5771 seems to be socially capable

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:47.800
of encouraging behavioral changes in humans.

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:53.990
Others have pointed out, much to Dr. Zaretsky’s
disdain, that 5771 is also highly lethal to

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:58.829
humans, perhaps as a contingency measure to
control population growth.

00:14:58.829 --> 00:15:04.040
Regardless, the Mushroom Man is to be kept
within Foundation containment indefinitely.

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:09.329
Interview sessions are ongoing, but it seems
unlikely that this SCP could ever be in nature

00:15:09.329 --> 00:15:14.150
again, no matter how much Dr. Zaretsky advocates
for it.

